PS5: recognize the x86_64-unknown-freebsd cross-compile host.

CPython's configure.ac only assigns ac_sys_system/_host_ident for a fixed
list of host triples when cross-compiling (the "for now, limit cross builds
to known configurations" case); anything else hits
AC_MSG_ERROR([cross build not supported for $host]) before reaching the
native-build MACHDEP fallback that already recognizes freebsd* via uname.
The PS5 SDK's host triple is x86_64-unknown-freebsd, so add explicit
*-*-freebsd* arms to both cross-build case statements (ac_sys_system and
_host_ident).

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -325,6 +325,9 @@ then
 	*-*-cygwin*)
 		ac_sys_system=Cygwin
 		;;
+	*-*-freebsd*)
+		ac_sys_system=FreeBSD
+		;;
 	*-apple-ios*)
 		ac_sys_system=iOS
 		;;
@@ -775,6 +778,9 @@ if test "$cross_compiling" = yes; then
 	*-*-cygwin*)
 		_host_ident=
 		;;
+	*-*-freebsd*)
+		_host_ident=$host_cpu
+		;;
 	*-*-darwin*)
 		;;
 	*-apple-ios*)
